data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"reasoning_content":"QA found a deviation: the Page component doesn't fill viewport height, and an extra wrapper div is used. The visual result is correct. DESIGN.md said \"The page content area fills the available viewport height between the header and footer\" and \"Inside Page, a Card centres the greeting and the button row.\" The implementation uses a wrapper div to achieve centering rather than Page itself.\n\nThe visual result is correct per QA. The question is whether this is acceptable. The design says \"No custom CSS should be needed beyond the design-system utilities and component classes; if inline layout is required, use the spacing tokens above.\" It does allow inline layout if required. And the wrapper uses spacing/flex tokens. So this is acceptable.\n\nAlso, the design said \"Inside Page, a Card centres the greeting and the buttons row.\" The Card is inside Page. The wrapper div is around Page, not inside. But the visual result matches.\n\nGiven the QA says the visual result is correct and all functional requirements pass, I should accept this with a note that the implementation deviated slightly from the exact component hierarchy but achieved the design intent.\n\nHowever, I need to consider: the design explicitly said the page content area fills available height. The implementation has a wrapper div around Page. Is this a failure? I think the intent is met. The Page component may not support filling height on its own, so the developer added a wrapper. This is reasonable.\n\nI'll accept qa. Then I need to merge the verified application into my branch and commit. My branch already has the application. But I should also fetch the QA's report perhaps? The orientation says merge the verified application. My branch already has it. I need to commit it (it's already committed from the fast-forward merges). \n\nBut wait - the QA's branch has report files. The orientation says \"Write durable results to ~/.local/share/cs-campaign/output\". I should write my own output. The QA's output is in their output dir. I don't need to merge QA's branch. I just need to accept their report and then finalize.\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Accept qa\n2. Confirm page still serves on 0.0.0.0:5173\n3. Reply to m1\n\nActually, the application is already merged into my branch and server is running. I need to ensure my branch is committed. It is (fast-forward to 0cf727b). I might want to add a final commit with any orchestrator notes, but not necessary.\n\nLet me also check the current git status and log."},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1789959988,"id":"chatcmpl-c5e4d5a4c92c44959400d256b1fa5681","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k2p7-code","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

